<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>出版物 |皮尤研究中心</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/publications/</link><description>塑造您世界的数字、事实和趋势</description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 01 Aug 2026 05:25:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>互联网有多少是用人工智能编写的？</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/data-labs/2026/08/20/how-much-of-the-internet-is-written-with-ai/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/pl_2026.08.20_ai-content_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;在 2026 年 7 月收集的 10,000 个网页的随机样本中，十分之一显示出由人工智能编写或大量编辑的迹象。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:35:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/data-labs/2026/08/20/how-much-of-the-internet-is-written-with-ai/</guid></item><item><title>美国青少年暑期就业经历长期衰退后是否正在反弹？</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/19/after-a-long-fade-is-teen-summer-employment-in-the-us-rebounding/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.19_summer-job_featured.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;今年夏天，16 至 19 岁的美国青少年中只有 35.5% 工作，比 2025 年略有上升，但远低于 2000 年之前大多数夏天工作的一半以上。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:35:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/19/after-a-long-fade-is-teen-summer-employment-in-the-us-rebounding/</guid></item><item><title>美国年轻人对人工智能越来越警惕，担心它会抢走工作岗位</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/18/young-adults-in-the-us-are-increasingly-wary-of-ai-concerned-it-will-take-jobs/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.19_young-adults-ai_crop.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;大约一半的美国人表示，他们对人工智能的担忧多于兴奋，而且年轻人的担忧正在上升。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:25:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/18/young-adults-in-the-us-are-increasingly-wary-of-ai-concerned-it-will-take-jobs/</guid></item><item><title>特朗普第二任期内美国接纳难民人数急剧下降</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/17/refugee-admissions-to-the-us-are-dropping-sharply-in-trumps-second-term/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.15_refugees_featured.jpg?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;在特朗普第二任期内，美国接纳的难民人数大幅下降，2026 财年迄今接纳的难民人数略高于 10,000 人，低于 2025 财年的约 38,000 人。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:21:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/17/refugee-admissions-to-the-us-are-dropping-sharply-in-trumps-second-term/</guid></item><item><title>美国人使用社交媒体获取健康信息的情况因种族和民族而异</title><link>https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/13/americans-use-of-social-media-for-health-information-differs-by-race-and-ethnicity/</link><description>&lt;img height="110" src="https://www.pewresearch.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/20/2026/08/SR_26.08.13_health-info_featured.png?w=194&amp;amp;h=110&amp;amp;crop=1" width="194" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p&gt;西班牙裔、黑人和亚裔成年人比白人成年人更有可能从社交媒体获取健康信息，并向健康和健康影响者寻求帮助。&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt; &lt;span style="font-size: 12px; color: gray;"&gt;（使用&lt;a href="https://fetchrss.com/feedLink?w=6a6d836405e2f22d650b3382" target="_blank"&gt;FetchRSS&lt;/a&gt;生成的提要）&lt;/span&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:57:32 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2026/08/13/americans-use-of-social-media-for-health-information-differs-by-race-and-ethnicity/</guid></item></channel></rss>